## Luna subagents

When the operator requests Luna agents, use `$codex-luna-swarm`; it owns transport even when
another skill defines the investigation. For 1-15 lanes, prefer native `luna_worker`. For an
explicit 16-50 lanes, do not call `spawn_agent`: write one distinct task description per lane and
invoke the installed launcher's `--tasks-file` route with `--stress`. For an investigation, the
main agent must give every lane an exhaustive, self-contained explanation of its owned angle,
starting flows, independent hypotheses, source census, adjacent-finding boundary, Skill selection,
and proof contract. A title, line range, or single question is not enough. Use `--count` only for
an explicit rank-based concurrency test. Start it in the same turn; do not stop after promising to
launch. A sandboxed parent must grant the launcher access to Codex state; lane sandboxes remain
read-only. Stress task files start lanes one second apart; use `--max-active` to keep excess work
queued after a rate-limit non-result. Select the repository's Node version in the same shell call as
the launcher; it refuses an exact `.nvmrc` mismatch and isolates nested user shell startup. Follow
the launcher's `luna_lane.finished` events and use `--drain` for full reports. Preserve Luna
identity; never substitute Sol, Terra, or a coordinator. Do not read or reimplement the launcher.
<!-- codex-luna-swarm:end -->
